Kompakt: USB serial: no wake-up on a closed tty

gs_start_io() woke port.tty without checking it. gs_start_rx() drops
port_lock, so a close on another CPU (the Kompakt app closing ttyGS0 as the
host configures ACM at plug-in) left it NULL and the phone panicked in
tty_wakeup(). Same fix as upstream Linux.

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
@@ -605,10 +605,15 @@
 	started = gs_start_rx(port);
 
 	if (started) {
+		struct tty_struct *tty;
+
 		gs_start_tx(port);
 		/* Unblock any pending writes into our circular buffer, in case
-		 * we didn't in gs_start_tx() */
-		tty_wakeup(port->port.tty);
+		 * we didn't in gs_start_tx(). gs_start_rx() drops port_lock, so
+		 * the tty may have been closed meanwhile. */
+		tty = port->port.tty;
+		if (tty)
+			tty_wakeup(tty);
 	} else {
 		gs_free_requests(ep, head, &port->read_allocated);
 		gs_free_requests(port->port_usb->in, &port->write_pool,
